integ5 0078 = patches/exl3p/0067-exl3p-prompt-experts-main-loop-and-epilogues.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

exl3p 0067: exl3 cuda: the prompt kernels' main loop compiled for an item's 8-member blocks, the next k tile decoded among the current MMAs, butterflies one FFMA, vector stores; the same bits

tf_exl3_prompt_gu / _down (and their _k6 twins) keep their items, blocks, B fragments and fp32 chains (each output one
chain of mma.m16n8k16 over the ascending k tiles from zero) and their epilogues' arithmetic; the main loop is fed
differently, after the K12 loop of patch 0073, patches/aevonix/0073 in Aevonix's GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-4x-RTX-PRO-6000-TensorFold:
- compiled for the item's 8-member column blocks (NBA 1..8, a switch on the count): no predicate, no MMA on a column block
  without a member, no member-row load nobody reads;
- two decoded A fragment sets: the next k tile's trellis decode issues among the current k tile's MMAs, across the stage
  barrier too (4 stages at shared rows, 3 at separate gate/up rows; both fit the existing static buffer);
- each thread's cp.async source and destination worked out once an item; the mcg mask in a register (an asm LOP3); 4-bit
  tiles decoded from the lane's word and its neighbour's in fewer shifts (decode_a8: lane_states<8>'s eight states).
Measured (GPU0 at 400 W, sustained, 2,048 rows, sigma 0.8 routing): gate/up 1.177x, down 1.161x, energy a call -9 to -10%.
SASS (nvcc 13.3, sm_120): a 32-K stage of the 4-bit gate/up loop 361 -> 210 (8 members) .. 243 (64) instructions,
down 331 -> 205 .. 238. Registers sm_120: gu 128 -> 122, down 127 -> 122, no spills, 2 blocks an SM, smem unchanged.
Checked byte for byte against 3f94715d's kernels (Xd and Y) at 3- and 4-bit, shared and separate rows, uniform,
skewed and crafted routing, 1 to 4,096 rows and every item size (opt/overnight/exl3p/tools/bench_p.cu).

Epilogues (after K12 too):
- fwht128f: fwht128's cross-lane butterfly v + o / o - v as fmaf(+1 or -1, v, o): s v is exact, so the FFMA rounds once
  as the add does (fwht128 compiles to an FSEL of -v and an FADD; after K12). Only the prompt epilogues use it; the
  shared fwht128 is unchanged. Gate/up's epilogue row 466 -> 396 instructions, down's 183..219 -> 142..163.
- Xd's 4 halves a lane in one 8-byte store, Y's 4 floats in one 16-byte store (the same values); Kernels.run refuses a y
  not 16-byte or an xd not 8-byte aligned (every caller's are: arena or slot rows of dims * 4 bytes).

